From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Kholodnyi <andrei.kholodnyi@windriver.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] env hooks: skip LD_LIBRARY_PATH library_path hook when
 cross-compiling

ament registers a per-package environment hook that prepends the package's
install `lib` dir to LD_LIBRARY_PATH. colcon sources the install base when it
assembles each package's build command environment, so for a cross-build the
VxWorks target install lib dir (full of target .so files -- libc.so.1,
libzstd.so.1, ...) lands on the HOST LD_LIBRARY_PATH during the build.

That entry is useless for a cross-build: the VxWorks compiler/linker resolve
target libs via -L/-rpath-link (toolchain / cc-conf), not LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and
the target runtime loader uses its own path config -- not the host
LD_LIBRARY_PATH. But it breaks any dynamically-linked HOST tool invoked during
the build (e.g. ccache, cargo's host build-script linker): the host loader
picks a VxWorks soname and fails to start:

  <tool>: error while loading shared libraries: libc.so.1: cannot open shared object file

Guard the hook on CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING so it is only emitted for native builds.
CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING is TRUE whenever CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME is set in the toolchain
(VxWorks here), so native builds are unaffected.
---
 ament_cmake_core/ament_cmake_environment_hooks-extras.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ament_cmake_core/ament_cmake_environment_hooks-extras.cmake b/ament_cmake_core/ament_cmake_environment_hooks-extras.cmake
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/ament_cmake_core/ament_cmake_environment_hooks-extras.cmake
+++ b/ament_cmake_core/ament_cmake_environment_hooks-extras.cmake
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ set(
 set(
   AMENT_CMAKE_ENVIRONMENT_HOOKS_DESC_ament_prefix_path
   "prepend-non-duplicate;AMENT_PREFIX_PATH;")
-if(NOT WIN32)
+if(NOT WIN32 AND NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
   if(NOT APPLE)
     set(
       AMENT_CMAKE_ENVIRONMENT_HOOKS_DESC_library_path
